+++ src/scanistry-5.0-25-source/usr/share/doc/scanistry/CHANGELOG-5.0-25	2026-10-24 21:43:55.053986196 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+Scanistry 5.0-25
+
+URLhaus: the retired keyless download is dropped, and URLhaus comes back with a free abuse.ch Auth-Key.
+
+Seen on a real machine (2026-10-24): every threat-feed refresh logged
+    Threat list download failed
+    https://urlhaus.abuse.ch/downloads/text/ could not be reached: HTTP Error 410: Gone
+    What to do: Check network connectivity. Scanistry retries automatically every 15 minutes; one list being briefly
+    unavailable is not a problem.
+and the refresh reached 2 of 3 sources. The network was fine. On 2026-10-23 abuse.ch stopped serving the URLhaus lists
+without an Auth-Key: /downloads/text/, /downloads/text_online/ and the other keyless addresses answer 410 Gone. Retrying
+could never succeed, and after 7 days the carried-forward copy (5.0-1) would have expired and URLhaus's entries would
+have dropped out.
+
+Configuration
+- New setting "urlhaus_auth_key" (default ""). Get a free key by signing in at https://auth.abuse.ch/ and generating an
+  Auth-Key, put it in /etc/scanistry/scanistry.conf, then: sudo systemctl restart scanistry. Scanistry then downloads
+  URLhaus's keyed export (https://urlhaus-api.abuse.ch/v2/files/exports/KEY/recent.csv) as a third source and keeps
+  the URLs it lists as online.
+- The key is never written to the log, feeds.json, feed-sources.json or the dashboard: they show
+  .../exports/(urlhaus_auth_key)/recent.csv, and error messages are scrubbed of it. A keyed export address pasted
+  into feed_urls is turned into urlhaus_auth_key for the same reason, with a warning. A malformed key (anything but
+  letters, digits, - and _, or not 16 to 128 characters) is refused with a warning, and URLhaus is skipped.
+- Any https://urlhaus.abuse.ch/downloads/... address in feed_urls is dropped when the configuration is read, with a
+  warning that says how to bring URLhaus back. Without a key, Scanistry uses Spamhaus DROP and Feodo Tracker, as
+  before, and "2 of 2 sources" is a clean refresh.
+- The shipped scanistry.conf no longer lists the URLhaus text address and has "urlhaus_auth_key": "". The postinst
+  migration removes the retired address from an existing scanistry.conf and adds the empty key, and prints how to
+  set it. It rewrites the file only when something changed, so running it again changes nothing.
+
+Downloads
+- The keyed export is a CSV with one row per URL (id, dateadded, url, url_status, ...). It has its own 64 MB ceiling
+  and a 300-second deadline. Every other feed keeps 8 MB and 120 seconds. Only the url column of rows marked
+  "online" is read. The urlhaus_link column (https://urlhaus.abuse.ch/url/N/) is never taken for a malware host.
+- A download that arrives as a ZIP archive is refused with a clear error rather than being parsed as text.
+- A source that fails keeps its last good copy for up to 7 days, as since 5.0-1.
+
+The Logs page
+- A feed that answers HTTP 404 or 410 is shown as "Threat list retired", and 401 or 403 as "Threat list refused the
+  download", with advice that fits: for the old URLhaus address, the Auth-Key steps; for the keyed export, check the
+  key; for any other list, change or remove it in feed_urls. Neither says to check network connectivity, because
+  retrying will not help. Timeouts, DNS errors and other failures keep the old "Threat list download failed" advice.
+  Lines already in the log from before the upgrade are explained the new way too.
+
+Help
+- The Threat Intelligence help names the default sources correctly and explains urlhaus_auth_key.
+
+Tests
+- New: tests/test_5025.py (no root needed): the retired addresses are dropped, the key adds the export and stays out
+  of every log line and state file (including an error that quotes the address), malformed keys, a pasted keyed
+  address, online and offline CSV rows, a refused key keeps the last good copy, and the Logs page wording for the
+  real 410 line, a 404, a 401 and a timeout. tests/test_feed_carry.py, check_broker.py, test_5017.py, test_5023.py and
+  test_5024.py still pass.
+
+Upgrading: sudo apt install ./scanistry_5.0-25_amd64.deb. Then, to keep URLhaus, add your Auth-Key as described above.
